./ ADD NAME=RDEFINE                                                             
)F FUNCTION -                                                                   
  The RDEFINE command defines a resource in a certain class.                    
  It writes one line in the PROFILES member of SYS1.SECURE.CNTL.                
                                                                                
  RDEFINE updates the control data sets on disk only.  Reload the in            
  core tables afterwards with 'S RAKFPROF' from the console, or by              
  running the RAKFPROF procedure in batch, or the profile is not in             
  effect.                                                                       
                                                                                
  You must be connected to the RAKFADM group. RDEFINE is an ordinary            
  problem state program - it is the protection on the control data sets         
  that enforces this, not APF authorization.                                    
                                                                                
)X SYNTAX -                                                                     
  RDEFINE 'resource' CLASS(clasname) UACC(NONE/READ/UPDATE/ALTER)               
                                                                                
  REQUIRED - 'resource'                                                         
           - CLASS(classname)                                                   
                                                                                
  DEFAULT  - UACC(NONE)                                                         
                                                                                
  EXAMPLE  - RDEFINE $TSTVS.* CLASS(FACILITY) UACC(READ)                        
                                                                                
  The operands can be shortened to the shortest unique abbreviation.            
  So, RDEFINE $TSTVS.* C(FACILITY) U(READ) is also valid.                       
                                                                                
  RETURN CODES:                                                                 
                                                                                
     0 - The resource is created.                                               
     8 - An error occurs. A suitable message will be given to                   
         the user.                                                              
)O OPERANDS -                                                                   
))'resource' - the generalized resource in the specified class. The             
  length can be up to 44 bytes. Generic resources can be created.               
))CLASS - Specify the name of the generalized resource class. The               
  class name is alphabetic value with a length up to 8 characters.              
))UACC - Specify the universal access of the resource.                          
  possible values are: NONE (no access), READ, UPDATE and                       
  ALTER (delete and create).                                                    
                                                                                
